From rgentlem at fhcrc.org  Thu Oct 20 00:03:56 2005
From: rgentlem at fhcrc.org (Robert Gentleman)
Date: Wed, 19 Oct 2005 15:03:56 -0700
Subject: [BioC] GO2PROBES
In-Reply-To: <002801c5d4f6$b489cbe0$8c987ca5@lurie.northwestern.edu>
References: <mailman.3.1129716000.30714.bioconductor@stat.math.ethz.ch>
	<002801c5d4f6$b489cbe0$8c987ca5@lurie.northwestern.edu>
Message-ID: <4356C2CC.2060508@fhcrc.org>

Good question, (it is GO2PROBE though, no S on that one)
   - basically the first maps between a GO ID and the set of probes that 
map to those genes for which the given GO ID is the most specific term 
that applies. The second, maps to all probes for which the GO ID is 
appropriate (and hence includes genes that have more specific functions 
than the selected GO ID). Our documentation on this is weak, and will be 
  improved for the next release.

   best wishes,
     Robert


